EXPERIMENT 16 – BASIC PERFORMANCE TESTING USING APACHE JMETER

AIM
To use Apache JMeter to execute a basic test plan using Thread Group, HTTP Request sampler and listeners.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Number of Threads = 5, Ramp-up Period = 5 seconds and Loop Count = 2.
4. Add an HTTP Request sampler and enter the website details.
5. Add View Results Tree and Summary Report listeners.
6. Save the plan as Exercise16.jmx and click Start.
7. Verify that the number of samples is 10.
TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	5
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	5 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	2
HTTP Request	Protocol	https
HTTP Request	Server Name	the-internet.herokuapp.com
HTTP Request	Method	GET
HTTP Request	Path	/
Listeners	Added	View Results Tree, Summary Report

INPUT
- Number of users: 5
- Loop count: 2
- Total samples: \(5 \times 2 = 10\)
- Website: https://the-internet.herokuapp.com
OUTPUT
Summary Report
Label	# Samples	Error %
Home Page	10	0.00%
TOTAL	10	0.00%

View Results Tree:
- All 10 samplers are green.
- Response code: 200
- Response message: OK
Average, minimum, maximum, standard deviation and throughput depend on your network and system.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to execute a basic test plan using Thread Group, HTTP Request sampler and listeners, and the results were verified.
